# Turnstile: Backend Architecture

**Project:** Turnstile
**Component:** Backend Server
**Status:** Draft
**Last Updated:** December 2025

---

## 1. Design Philosophy

Turnstile backend is a **thin proxy layer**. It forwards requests to the Orchestrator and streams responses back to the frontend. No business logic, no state management, no LLM calls.

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|----------------|
| **Stateless** | No session storage, no persistence |
| **Proxy only** | Forward requests to Orchestrator |
| **Stream-through** | Pass SSE from Orchestrator to frontend |
| **Minimal** | Only exists for CORS and static serving |

---

## 2. Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        Frontend                              │
│                   (React + Vite)                             │
│                   localhost:5173                             │
└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   Turnstile Backend                          │
│                    localhost:3001                            │
│                                                              │
│  • Proxy /api/chat to Orchestrator                           │
│  • Stream SSE responses                                      │
│  • Serve static files (production)                           │
│  • CORS handling                                             │
│                                                              │
└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      ORCHESTRATOR                            │
│                    localhost:3006                            │
│                                                              │
│  Executes pipelines, coordinates services via SAK            │
│                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Endpoints

| Turnstile Endpoint | Orchestrator Endpoint | Purpose |
|--------------------|----------------------|---------|
| `POST /api/chat` | `POST /orchestrate/whitepaper-chat` | Send message, receive stream |
| `POST /api/sessions` | `POST /orchestrate/create-session` | Create new session |
| `GET /api/sessions/:id` | `GET /orchestrate/session/:id` | Get session turns |

---

## 4. Implementation

### 4.1 Server Setup

```typescript
// server.ts
import express from "express";
import cors from "cors";
import { config } from "./config";

const app = express();

app.use(cors({ origin: config.corsOrigin }));
app.use(express.json());

// Proxy routes
app.use("/api", proxyRouter);

// Static files (production)
app.use(express.static("dist"));

app.listen(config.port, () => {
  console.log(`Turnstile backend on port ${config.port}`);
});
```

### 4.2 Chat Proxy (Streaming)

```typescript
// routes/proxy.ts
import { Router } from "express";
import { config } from "../config";

const router = Router();

router.post("/chat", async (req, res) => {
  const { message, session_id } = req.body;

  const response = await fetch(`${config.orchestratorUrl}/orchestrate/whitepaper-chat`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify({ message, session_id }),
  });

  // Stream SSE response
  res.setHeader("Content-Type", "text/event-stream");
  res.setHeader("Cache-Control", "no-cache");
  res.setHeader("Connection", "keep-alive");

  const reader = response.body?.getReader();
  if (!reader) {
    res.status(502).end();
    return;
  }

  const decoder = new TextDecoder();
  while (true) {
    const { done, value } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    res.write(decoder.decode(value));
  }
  res.end();
});

router.post("/sessions", async (req, res) => {
  const response = await fetch(`${config.orchestratorUrl}/orchestrate/create-session`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(req.body),
  });
  res.status(response.status).json(await response.json());
});

router.get("/sessions/:id", async (req, res) => {
  const response = await fetch(`${config.orchestratorUrl}/orchestrate/session/${req.params.id}`);
  res.status(response.status).json(await response.json());
});

export default router;
```

